    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are the 10 things to evaluate when hiring a LinkedIn personal branding agency for Founders + CEOs + MDs?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Named industry client work (verifiable case studies + LinkedIn URLs). (2) Regulated firms (SEBI-listed, RBI-regulated) require board/compliance review; no misleading forward-looking financial statements; investor-relations content aligned with disclosures familiarity + compliance review workflow. (3) Voice-capture ghostwriting quality — sample writing that sounds like you. (4) Content velocity (10-25+ posts/month at Growth+ tier). (5) Team + pod structure (dedicated senior account manager, not junior fill-in). (6) Video + Reels + LinkedIn Live production capability. (7) Newsletter + Creator Mode + LinkedIn Live expertise. (8) Sales Navigator + LinkedIn Ads management. (9) Contract terms — MSA length, cancellation clauses, IP ownership. (10) Attribution reporting + monthly ROI transparency.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What red flags should we watch for in LinkedIn agencies?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Guaranteed follower/lead numbers — LinkedIn agencies can't guarantee outcomes, only quality of execution. (2) Bulk/generic content templates — kills authenticity. (3) No named client work + unverifiable portfolio. (4) 12-24 month lock-in contracts with no cancellation. (5) 'We use AI to write everything' — LinkedIn algorithm penalizes AI-generated content; industry peers detect it instantly. (6) No industry expertise for Founders + CEOs + MDs. (7) No compliance review workflow — creates firm risk. (8) Package pricing hidden or 'contact us' only. (9) Weak attribution reporting. (10) Junior team-only staffing on senior accounts.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are fair contract terms for LinkedIn agency engagements?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Standard 6-month Master Service Agreement (MSA) with cancellation option after month 3 if agreed milestones not met — protects both sides. Monthly retainer + agreed deliverables. Ad-spend (LinkedIn Ads) transparent pass-through — no markup. IP ownership 100% client on creative + content library + Sales Nav lists + WhatsApp automation + customer data. Notice period 30-60 days. Non-solicitation clause reasonable. Avoid: 12-24 month lock-ins, IP-retention clauses, hidden ad-spend markup, unclear termination terms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How much should a LinkedIn personal branding agency cost per month?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For Founders + CEOs + MDs in India + GCC: Starter Rs 30,000-40,000/mo, Growth Rs 40,000-70,000/mo, Premium Rs 60,000-1,00,000/mo, Enterprise Rs 1,20,000-3,00,000/mo. Anyone charging <Rs 20,000/mo — likely freelance-quality without industry expertise + compliance. Anyone charging >Rs 4,00,000/mo without dedicated 8-10 person pod — likely padded. ITD's transparent pricing: Rs 30K / 40K / 60K / 1.2L across 4 tiers. See <a href='/services/linkedin-personal-branding.php#packages'>packages</a>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Should the LinkedIn agency understand our industry specifically?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Yes — critical. For Founder/CEO, Managing Director, Chief Executive, Co-founder, Executive Chairman, Second-generation family-business CEO, industry-native writing + industry-specific content angles + Regulated firms (SEBI-listed, RBI-regulated) require board/compliance review; no misleading forward-looking financial statements; investor-relations content aligned with disclosures familiarity are non-negotiable. Generic content agencies can produce grammatically correct posts, but peer Founders + CEOs + MDs instantly detect non-native industry language. Vet by asking: (1) Have they worked with Founders + CEOs + MDs before? (2) Sample writing for a mock scenario in your industry. (3) Do they know Regulated firms (SEBI-listed, RBI-regulated) require board/compliance review; no misleading forward-looking financial statements; investor-relations content aligned with disclosures? ITD specializes in banking + real estate + B2B manufacturing + SaaS/tech + consulting/PE-VC verticals.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we test agency quality before signing a contract?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">3 tests: (1) Sample content — ask agency to write 2 sample LinkedIn posts based on a 15-min brief. Evaluate: voice authenticity, industry vocabulary, compliance-safety, engagement-worthiness. (2) Client references — request 2-3 named client references. Ask references: response time, work quality, willingness to renew. (3) Trial engagement — 30-day pilot at reduced scope before committing to 6-month MSA. ITD offers all 3 during onboarding.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What should the first-90-day plan look like?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Standard 90-day plan from a competent LinkedIn agency: <strong>Days 1-30 (Foundation):</strong> 60-min voice-capture interview, profile optimization (About + banner + headline + Featured), Sales Nav setup, editorial calendar for first 60 days, first 8-12 posts published. <strong>Days 31-60 (Publish + Iterate):</strong> Weekly briefs established, video/Reels production started, newsletter setup, first monthly performance review, engagement + community management active. <strong>Days 61-90 (Scale + Measure):</strong> Content velocity at target level, Sales Nav outreach active (Premium+), first inbound qualified DMs, quarterly business review + strategy adjustment.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What if we don't like the agency after 3 months?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Standard 6-month MSA with cancellation after month 3 protects both sides. If unhappy at month 3: raise specific concerns in writing (creative quality, response time, missed deliverables). Agency has 30 days to remediate. If unresolved, cancellation clause activates. Notice period 30-60 days. Final month deliverables completed, IP transferred, Sales Nav lists exported, content library archived to client. ITD's cancellation clause: month 3 no-fault exit if milestones missed. See <a href='/services/linkedin-personal-branding.php'>service page</a>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we integrate an external LinkedIn agency with our internal team?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">3-layer integration: (1) Executive assistant / marketing manager on client side coordinates weekly briefs, reviews content, manages calendar coordination with agency. (2) CRM/inbox integration — qualified LinkedIn DMs flow to client's CRM/sales team within 15 min. (3) Firm compliance officer (for regulated industries) reviews content pre-publish (agency pre-flags compliance-adjacent content). Weekly 15-min sync call between client + agency account manager. Monthly performance review call. Quarterly business review with client + agency senior partner.</div>
